    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b43f694_4e5e57f7",
        "filename": "common/panic_output.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 585,
      "author": {
        "id": 1479762
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-03T00:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this flag is pretty much ignored in the ectool and used to determine if panicinfo is new or old in platform2/libec. I\u0027m not sure if we want to use it for a different meaning. Best way to understand if the chunk is a last one is to check that `PANIC_DATA_FLAG_TRUNCATED` is NOT set.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 585,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 585,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "270cb4e1b23dabe6c302de481b5afbfcd3765a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2aef3b5_0d07b485",
        "filename": "common/panic_output.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 585,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-07T20:31:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`PANIC_DATA_FLAG_TRUNCATED` cannot be used. The flag field is at the start of the struct so it is read first.\n\nectool does ignore it, however it not ignored by the crash reporter. This flag indicates if the panic is old or new.",
      "parentUuid": "9b43f694_4e5e57f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 585,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 585,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "270cb4e1b23dabe6c302de481b5afbfcd3765a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a884bd26_43afaef9",
        "filename": "include/panic_defs.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 178,
      "author": {
        "id": 1479762
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-03T00:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t that flag more suitable to use rather than `PANIC_DATA_FLAG_OLD_HOSTCMD` ?",
      "revId": "270cb4e1b23dabe6c302de481b5afbfcd3765a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94dce6cc_adac1bd5",
        "filename": "include/panic_defs.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 178,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-07T20:31:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PANIC_DATA_FLAG_TRUNCATED is set when the panic data is too large for the host command. With v2, this is no longer needed, since the host is expected to keep reading the panic_data until the whole struct is read.",
      "parentUuid": "a884bd26_43afaef9",
      "revId": "270cb4e1b23dabe6c302de481b5afbfcd3765a0b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ]
